      "writtenOn": "2024-05-01T21:56:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Security callbacks are registered when a security process is requested for a service. It is mostly for the encryption request to meet the security requirements of the service.\nOn rare occasions the service access may result in pairing if the link was not already paired. In such a case, the disconnection on the other transport would lead to pairing failure.\n\nEg. `l2c_link_sec_comp()`, `rfc_sec_check_complete()`, `l2cble_sec_comp()`.\nLater two appear to be ignoring the transport.",
